## Security Testing

```typescript
// ✅ Test authentication enforcement
describe('Authentication', () => {
  it('returns 401 when no auth token is provided', async () => {
    const response = await app.request('/api/v1/users', { method: 'GET' });
    expect(response.status).toBe(401);
  });

  it('returns 401 when token is expired', async () => {
    const expiredToken = generateToken({ userId: 'user-1' }, { expiresIn: '-1h' });
    const response = await app.request('/api/v1/users', {
      headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${expiredToken}` },
    });
    expect(response.status).toBe(401);
  });

  it('returns 401 when token is malformed', async () => {
    const response = await app.request('/api/v1/users', {
      headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer not.a.valid.token' },
    });
    expect(response.status).toBe(401);
  });
});

// ✅ Test authorization (role-based access)
describe('Authorization', () => {
  it('returns 403 when non-admin tries to delete a user', async () => {
    const viewerToken = generateToken({ userId: 'user-1', role: 'viewer' });
    const response = await app.request('/api/v1/users/user-2', {
      method: 'DELETE',
      headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${viewerToken}` },
    });
    expect(response.status).toBe(403);
  });

  it('prevents users from accessing other users\' private data', async () => {
    const userToken = generateToken({ userId: 'user-1', role: 'viewer' });
    const response = await app.request('/api/v1/users/user-2/private', {
      headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${userToken}` },
    });
    expect(response.status).toBe(403);
  });
});

// ✅ Test input validation (injection prevention)
describe('Input Validation', () => {
  it('rejects SQL injection in query parameters', async () => {
    const response = await app.request('/api/v1/users?status=active\'; DROP TABLE users;--');
    expect(response.status).toBe(400);
  });

  it('rejects XSS payloads in request body', async () => {
    const response = await app.request('/api/v1/posts', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', Authorization: `Bearer ${adminToken}` },
      body: JSON.stringify({ title: '<script>alert("xss")</script>', content: 'Test' }),
    });
    const body = await response.json();
    // Should either reject or sanitize — never store raw HTML
    expect(body.data?.title).not.toContain('<script>');
  });

  it('enforces maximum input lengths', async () => {
    const response = await app.request('/api/v1/users', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      body: JSON.stringify({ email: 'a@b.c', name: 'x'.repeat(1000) }),
    });
    expect(response.status).toBe(400);
  });
});
```

**Security Testing Rules:**
- Test ALL endpoints without auth tokens → expect `401`.
- Test ALL admin endpoints with non-admin tokens → expect `403`.
- Test boundary inputs: empty strings, very long strings, special characters, SQL/XSS payloads.
- Test that sensitive fields (`password`, `token`) are NEVER present in API responses.
- Include security tests in CI — they must pass before every deployment.

